---
// The claim, in one statement. Between the words sit the app's own parts, drawn at the size of
// the type and in the page's colours: the Reviewer's Verified and the red Add of an add-on's card. Each part stays on the
// line of the word after it. The spaces are written out: Astro's compression drops a line break
// that sits between text and a tag.
import { home } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="intro" data-tone="paper" aria-label="What it is">
  <!-- Where the sea can't part (no WebGL, or reduced motion), the home window sits here instead. -->
  <img class="intro__home" src="/media/mac-working-1400.webp" srcset="/media/mac-working-1400.webp 1400w, /media/mac-working.webp 2400w"
    sizes="min(92vw, 1100px)" alt={home.alt} width="2400" height="1414" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
  <p class="intro__text" data-reveal="focus">
    It runs Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Hermes together: one leads, a quicker one takes the routine work, one from another maker{' '}
    <span class="intro__pair"><span class="inl inl--ok" aria-hidden="true"><span class="inl__dot"></span>Verified</span> checks.</span>{' '}
    What it lacks, they make as{' '}
    <span class="intro__pair"><span class="inl inl--act" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>Add</span> add-ons</span>{' '}
    you say yes to.
  </p>
</section>
